{
  "$comment": "McBylaw scope rules and TOC page rules (Spec 68 §6.4 rules 1-2 and 11, §9 G-UNIVERSE, §10 stage 3; Spec 69 M-31, M-37, M-47). AUTHORED RULES, applied by scripts/analysis/bylaw/universe.mjs. Rows: every sliced row resolves to exactly one rule: the lowest tier that matches wins; two matching rules in one tier is a failure (scope_ambiguous); no rule is a failure (scope_unmatched). Tiers: 1 mechanical (deleted slots) · 2 page_status (retired pages, ruled) · 3 administrative (M-31: after mechanical, before everything else) · 4 other judgment reasons · 5 definitions (mechanical, by the declared matcher) · 6 page_scope (the in-scope default of a pinned page). A judgment rule whose `ruling` is null is PROPOSED: its rows are `awaiting_ruling` (counted) until the operator rules and `--accept --ruling=<id>` pins the universe. Match keys are ANDed; each key is an OR list. Evidence: every row a mechanical or judgment rule matches must contain one of its `evidence` patterns (case-insensitive, >= 2 words), else scope_evidence_missing. Counts are never written here: they are computed from the slice (universe.lock.json pins them).",
  "version": 1,
